# tests/audio/KINDCLASS - the maximum class of every audio row kind (plan 05-05; D-208, ER-17, F-73e): KIND, a TAB, the ceiling, a TAB and the form the kind takes. scripts/audio-check reads it (AEXP_CLASS_INFLATED) and the runner kind audio knows the same kinds (tests/conformance/audiokinds.c).
# Ceiling rule (a page-set rule): a group's MAN labels must be a subset of the ceiling's labels (a narrower set is fine); GUEST only where the ceiling is GUEST or MAN; ASSUMED always; DEF (a definition, ER-19) only where the ceiling is DEF.
# P8-10 is in the period and live sets for the S = 4 rows of 05-06, and P8-2 in the same set for r7_ignored (plan check 1 warning 4). Each later plan checks its rows against these sets with audio-check before its commit; a row a set does not admit is a recorded deviation, never a silent widening.
